.TH LUS-TEST 1 "" "Lus" "Lus Manual"
.SH NAME
lus-test \- run the tests of a project
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBlus test\fR [options] [path ...]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs the tests in the named files, or in every \fB*_test.lus\fR file inside the named directories.
A plain run also calls each benchmark once.
With no path, it searches the current directory.
Files run in parallel, each in its own process and temporary directory.
Testing describes how to write tests.
.PP
The exit status is 0 when every file passes, 1 when a test fails or a file cannot run, and 2 when a named path does not exist.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-filter TEXT\fR
Run only the tests whose names contain \fBTEXT\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-list\fR
Print \fBFILE: NAME\fR for each test and benchmark that the run would start, without running them.
With \fB\-\-json\fR, print one record per name with the fields \fBfile\fR, \fBname\fR, and \fBkind\fR.
.TP
\fB\-u\fR, \fB\-\-update\fR
Rewrite the snapshots that no longer match.
With \fB\-\-bench\fR, save the results as the baseline.
.TP
\fB\-\-bench\fR
Measure the functions whose names end in \fB_bench\fR and compare them with the saved baseline, in place of running the tests.
Benchmarks describes the measurement.
.TP
\fB\-\-bench\-time S\fR
Measure each benchmark for S seconds.
The default is 1.
.TP
\fB\-\-coverage\fR
Report which lines of the code under test ran.
Coverage describes the report.
.TP
\fB\-\-coverage\-out FILE\fR
Also write the coverage to FILE as an lcov tracefile, which editors and coverage services read.
.TP
\fB\-\-doc\fR
Run the \fB \fR`\fBlus \fR code blocks of Markdown files and of the doc comments of \fB.lus\fR files in place of test files, which keeps the examples of documentation correct.
.TP
\fB\-v\fR
List the skipped tests of passing files too.
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print one JSON record per test, for other tools to read.
.TP
\fB\-\-jobs N\fR
Run at most N files at once.
The default is the number of processors, or 1 with \fB\-\-bench\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-timeout S\fR
Stop a file that writes no output for S seconds.
The default is 60.
.TP
\fB\-\-file\-timeout S\fR
Stop a file that runs longer than S seconds in all.
The default is ten times the timeout.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
0
Every file passed.
.TP
1
A test failed or a file could not run.
.TP
2
A named path does not exist or an option is malformed.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lus (1)
.PP
The CLI page of the Lus manual, https://lus.dev/manual/cli#lus-test, has the same text with links to the rest of the manual.
